===Alternative forms===
* [[trepeget]] {{qualifier|obsolete}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fro}} {{term|trebuchet|lang=fro}}, {{term|trebuket}} et al. (modern {{term|trébuchet|lang=fr}}), from {{term|trebuchier||to overthrow, topple|lang=fro}}, from {{term|tre-|lang=fro}} + {{recons|buchier|buchier|lang=fro}}, from {{etyl|fro}} {{term|buc||trunk of the body|lang=fro}}, from Old {{etyl|frk}} {{recons|buk|būk|belly, trunk, torso|lang=frk}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{recons|būkaz||belly, abdomen, trunk|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{recons|bʰōw-||to blow, swell|lang=ine-pro}}. Cognate with {{etyl|goh|-}} {{term|buh|būh|belly|lang=goh}}, {{etyl|ang|-}} {{term|buc|būc|belly, trunk|lang=ang}}. More at {{l|en|bouk}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈtɹɛbəʃɛt/|/ˈtɹɛb.jə.ʃeɪ/|/ˈtɹɛb.ju.ʃeɪ/}}; {{X-SAMPA|/"trEb.j@.SeI/|/"trEb.jU.SeI/}}
* {{a|US}} {{enPR|trěb’yo͞o-shet}}, {{IPA|/ˈtɹɛb.juˌʃɛt/|/ˈtɹɛb.jəˌʃeɪ/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A medieval [[siege engine]] consisting of a large pivoting arm heavily weighted on one end. Considered to be the technological successor to the [[catapult]].
# A [[torture]] device for [[dunk]]ing suspected [[witch]]es by means of a [[chair]] attached to the end of a long pole.

